Conclusion and Outlook:
Implemented anisotorpic tension compression split in Pace3D in C programming language. Details of pace3d (Multiphysics software packagae at IAM-MMS, highly parallelized, with 600k+ lines of code). Validated the implementation using simulation benchmark cases. Discussion of take home messages from this work. This work will enable modeling of physically realistic crack phenomenon in anisotropic elastic materials., which was previously missing in pace3D.

Outlook on what could be achieved now. 
Extension to plasticity, thermal, and chemical effects. Battery electrodes have ansitropic elastic properties.